["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"DNA Repair Is the Key to Long Life: A Bowhead Whale Repair Protein Is Already in Human Trials New work finds that nearly half of hospitalized COVID-19 patients had dormant viruses reactivate in their bodies, with higher inflammation and cell damage a year later; meanwhile what long-lived animals like the bowhead whale share is not tumor-suppressor genes but stronger DNA repair, and drugs built on that idea have reached human trials. Nature Podcast Nature Podcast Briefing Chat: Is DNA repair the secret to a long life? Whales and mole-rats offer tantalizing hints Long COVID Dormant viruses DNA repair Anti-aging Human trials Bowhead whales dormant virus double-strand break CIRBP (cold-inducible RNA-binding protein) Sirt6 Fucoidan NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-07-naturepod-長新冠或源於休眠病毒-dna修復或為長壽關鍵/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/61b9f3b71a8cbe675f3cedcb/1786105817525-2bb986fa-0e50-42e5-a5cd-1ab1f3bc9517.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">13:52</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Nature Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0807</span></div>\n<h2>DNA Repair Is the Key to Long Life: A Bowhead Whale Repair Protein Is Already in Human Trials</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">New work finds that nearly half of hospitalized COVID-19 patients had dormant viruses reactivate in their bodies, with higher inflammation and cell damage a year later; meanwhile what long-lived animals like the bowhead whale share is not tumor-suppressor genes but stronger DNA repair, and drugs built on that idea have reached human trials.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Long COVID</span><span class=\"tag\">Dormant viruses</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"Don&#x27;t Teach Your Kid Empathy; First Let Them See You Listening Getting kids to disagree well is not a matter of teaching empathy or perspective-taking — it is a matter of proving with words that you are listening; the HEAR framework and the curiosity sandwich can be used immediately. Raising Good Humans Raising Good Humans How to Disagree With Your Kids Without Fighting Parent-child talk Disagreement Listening Harvard research Conversation frameworks Parenting HEAR framework curiosity sandwich false polarization hedging\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-07-raisinggh-別只讓孩子換位思考-要讓他看見你在聽/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/64875c2a-9023-11f1-b6bf-e7aff692fa61/image/dca88085db0b2fe33b742b29ede07799.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"R\"><span class=\"dur\">55:22</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Raising Good Humans</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0807</span></div>\n<h2>Don&#x27;t Teach Your Kid Empathy; First Let Them See You Listening</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Getting kids to disagree well is not a matter of teaching empathy or perspective-taking — it is a matter of proving with words that you are listening; the HEAR framework and the curiosity sandwich can be used immediately.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Parent-child talk</span><span class=\"tag\">Disagreement</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Screening embryos isn&#x27;t doing everything possible — it&#x27;s moral blackmail Genetic screening can lower disease risk, but the statistics are routinely oversold, and the practice may deepen social inequality. Parents should aim for &quot;good enough&quot; rather than optimal, and stay wary of the moral blackmail commercial firms trade on. The Gray Area with Sean Illing The Gray Area What does a parent owe their child? Genetic screening Reproductive ethics IVF Polygenic testing Value pluralism PGT-A polygenic testing pleiotropy satisficing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-07-grayarea-胚胎篩選-父母該為孩子做到哪一步/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/a4ca29cc-381a-11f1-a32d-c7b32dc2aeff/image/09d3576515488959f432d219d5c7416b.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">27:47</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Gray Area with Sean Illing</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0807</span></div>\n<h2>Screening embryos isn&#x27;t doing everything possible — it&#x27;s moral blackmail</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Genetic screening can lower disease risk, but the statistics are routinely oversold, and the practice may deepen social inequality. Parents should aim for &quot;good enough&quot; rather than optimal, and stay wary of the moral blackmail commercial firms trade on.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Genetic screening</span><span class=\"tag\">Reproductive ethics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"An Actress&#x27;s Contract Locked In Her Body: Gain Weight and You Breach It, Lose Weight and It Kills You In the 1920s the actress Molly was shelved by her studio for gaining weight and ended up on an operating table; in the 1990s a bride named Mary died from the diet drug fen-phen. Once a body becomes a commercial asset, the punishment and the shortcut lead to the same place. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales The Weight of Fame: A Hollywood Tragedy Hollywood Body standards Diet drugs Business ethics Contract terms Medical risk lipectomy fen-phen primary pulmonary hypertension (PPH)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-07-cautionary-製片廠的合同裡寫著-女演員的身體不得改變/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/c0ae8c6e-22f0-4e9b-ac1c-ae390037ac53/7f5a4714-6b10-4ccf-a424-ae390037ac70/image.jpg?t=1650471153&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">41:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0807</span></div>\n<h2>An Actress&#x27;s Contract Locked In Her Body: Gain Weight and You Breach It, Lose Weight and It Kills You</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In the 1920s the actress Molly was shelved by her studio for gaining weight and ended up on an operating table; in the 1990s a bride named Mary died from the diet drug fen-phen. Once a body becomes a commercial asset, the punishment and the shortcut lead to the same place.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Hollywood</span><span class=\"tag\">Body standards</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AMD Buys Talus: Burning AI Models Into Silicon, 17,000 Tokens a Second AMD has acquired Talus, a startup that builds custom chips for one specific AI model each and reaches 17,000 tokens per second. It marks a turn in AI inference toward non-programmable, model-specific silicon. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato Why did AMD just buy this REALLY WEIRD chip company? AI chips AMD Talus Model customization Inference acceleration SRAM reticle size agentic AI\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-06-techtechpotato-amd收購talus-押注模型定製芯片的未來/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/3MKRjt59hh4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">16:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0806</span></div>\n<h2>AMD Buys Talus: Burning AI Models Into Silicon, 17,000 Tokens a Second</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AMD has acquired Talus, a startup that builds custom chips for one specific AI model each and reaches 17,000 tokens per second. It marks a turn in AI inference toward non-programmable, model-specific silicon.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI chips</span><span class=\"tag\">AMD</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"AI Didn&#x27;t Kill Jobs — Agent Teamwork Is the Real Bottleneck Yangqing Jia (賈揚清) traces fifteen years of AI from Caffe through two startups: model capability is already good enough, and the bottleneck is getting a group of agents to collaborate the way a human team does. He also argues flatly that AI has not caused mass layoffs — it is just the scapegoat. What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道 科技早知道 賈揚清：我所經歷的「人工智能已死」到「AI 顛覆世界」的數年鉅變丨串臺「聲東擊西」S10E24 AI Startups Open source Agents Silicon Valley LLMs Caffe AlexNet Agent FAIR\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-06-whatsnext-單個智能體再強也成不了團隊-ai需要生產關係/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://media24.fireside.fm/file/fireside-images-2024/podcasts/images/4/4931937e-0184-4c61-a658-6b03c254754d/cover.jpg?v=10\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"W\"><span class=\"dur\">2:10:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">What&#x27;s Next｜科技早知道</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0806</span></div>\n<h2>AI Didn&#x27;t Kill Jobs — Agent Teamwork Is the Real Bottleneck</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Yangqing Jia (<span lang=\"zh\">賈揚清</span>) traces fifteen years of AI from Caffe through two startups: model capability is already good enough, and the bottleneck is getting a group of agents to collaborate the way a human team does. He also argues flatly that AI has not caused mass layoffs — it is just the scapegoat.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Startups</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Yo-yo dieting doesn&#x27;t wreck your metabolism; habits, not weight, decide lifespan Weight cycling — yo-yo dieting — does not permanently break your metabolism, and in ordinary people the weight that comes back rarely costs you muscle. What actually shapes health and lifespan is the healthy habits themselves, not the swings in weight. Science Vs Science Vs Weight Loss: Why Won&#x27;t It Stick? Weight cycling Weight loss Metabolism Inflammation Healthy habits Randomized trials weight cycling visceral fat macrophage\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-06-sciencevs-體重循環不毀代謝-健康行為比體重重要/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/f521b120-2c30-11e6-b5f3-63ee984ee1a4/image/e7470287efbfa0aff068175bb6c31805.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">39:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0806</span></div>\n<h2>Yo-yo dieting doesn&#x27;t wreck your metabolism; habits, not weight, decide lifespan</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Weight cycling — yo-yo dieting — does not permanently break your metabolism, and in ordinary people the weight that comes back rarely costs you muscle. What actually shapes health and lifespan is the healthy habits themselves, not the swings in weight.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Weight cycling</span><span class=\"tag\">Weight loss</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The US joins Japan to intervene on the yen: selling euros, not dollars, and betting the BOJ hikes In a rare move, the US Treasury has intervened on the yen alongside Japan, selling euros rather than dollars and putting the FIMA repo facility to use. Brad Setser argues the intervention will work as long as the Bank of Japan raises rates, and that Japan&#x27;s fiscal position is far better than America&#x27;s. Odd Lots Odd Lots Brad Setser on the US&#x27;s Unusual Japanese Yen Intervention Yen FX intervention Bank of Japan Treasuries Fiscal policy FIMA Repo Facility ESF (Exchange Stabilization Fund) Primary Balance Carry Trade Big Mac Index\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-06-oddlots-美國為何聯手日本干預日元-新工具與舊邏輯/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">42:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0806</span></div>\n<h2>The US joins Japan to intervene on the yen: selling euros, not dollars, and betting the BOJ hikes</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In a rare move, the US Treasury has intervened on the yen alongside Japan, selling euros rather than dollars and putting the FIMA repo facility to use. Brad Setser argues the intervention will work as long as the Bank of Japan raises rates, and that Japan&#x27;s fiscal position is far better than America&#x27;s.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Yen</span><span class=\"tag\">FX intervention</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"222-nanometre lamps kill pathogens and still sell a few hundred a year; the bottleneck isn&#x27;t the technology Far UVC uses 222-nanometre light to inactivate pathogens in the air while leaving the outer layer of human tissue unharmed; a South African TB trial is already seeing 90% suppression, yet the whole world buys only a few hundred units a year. The real bottleneck is how far the knowledge has spread. Complex Systems Complex Systems The economics of putting germicidal light in every room, with Misha Gurevich and Vivian Belenky of Aerolamp far UVC airborne disease public health startups building codes cost curves far UVC krypton chloride excimer lamp ASHRAE 241 R0 hygiene hypothesis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-06-complexsys-222納米殺菌燈便宜有效-缺的是認知而非技術/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://img.transistorcdn.com/_SmyPmSli4we-X2h7KiJ-wvjf2umakfC-X_hqszS_rE/rs:fill:0:0:1/w:1400/h:1400/q:60/mb:500000/aHR0cHM6Ly9pbWct/dXBsb2FkLXByb2R1/Y3Rpb24udHJhbnNp/c3Rvci5mbS8xMTZi/ODRmODgzZTZiNjAz/N2YzNmQxY2RkY2M4/YTE0Ni5wbmc.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:16:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Complex Systems</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0806</span></div>\n<h2>222-nanometre lamps kill pathogens and still sell a few hundred a year; the bottleneck isn&#x27;t the technology</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Far UVC uses 222-nanometre light to inactivate pathogens in the air while leaving the outer layer of human tissue unharmed; a South African TB trial is already seeing 90% suppression, yet the whole world buys only a few hundred units a year. The real bottleneck is how far the knowledge has spread.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">far UVC</span><span class=\"tag\">airborne disease</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"The Soviet Union forged its women into supermen and spoiled its men into uselessness 27 million Soviet citizens died in the Second World War, and men became a scarce resource; the state used an abortion ban, rewards for children fathered outside marriage, and the decriminalization of domestic violence to forge its women into supermen and spoil its men into uselessness — an order that still underwrites Putin&#x27;s patriarchal mobilization. Conversations with Tyler Conversations with Tyler Julia Ioffe on Russian Women, Missing Men, and the Roots of Autocracy Russian society Gender politics Population policy Feminist history Putin politics woman question single sex family gender essentialism pronatalist policy steam valve\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-05-tyler-蘇聯把女人煉成超人-把男人寵成廢物/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/9/3/b/c/93bcc9e054e0ad4fd959afa2a1bf1c87/JuliaIoffe-libsyn-20260804-lpkt75rsui.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">55:14</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Conversations with Tyler</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0805</span></div>\n<h2>The Soviet Union forged its women into supermen and spoiled its men into uselessness</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">27 million Soviet citizens died in the Second World War, and men became a scarce resource; the state used an abortion ban, rewards for children fathered outside marriage, and the decriminalization of domestic violence to forge its women into supermen and spoil its men into uselessness — an order that still underwrites Putin&#x27;s patriarchal mobilization.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Russian society</span><span class=\"tag\">Gender politics</span>\n</div></div></a>"]